  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urban Nature CONEXUS: co-producing regeneration ecosystems nexus for urban sustainability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project (led by the University of Sheffield) is addressed to structure, coordinate and promote access to shared, contextualised knowledge needed to support cities and communities to co-create NBS and restore urban ecosystems for increased urban resilience and urban dwellers&apos; quality of life.
Objective 1: Catalyse NBS partnerships between EU and CELAC cities.
Objective 2: Build a shared understanding of NBS and their local and wider contexts in EU and CELAC cities.
Objective 3: Develop local partnerships and foster participatory engagement to identify, initiate and co-create NBS interventions, and to embed NBS into urban plans and policies at multiple scales. 
Objective 4: Strengthen the rationales and narratives underpinning the implementation and creation of NBS.
Objective 5: Engage with businesses and communities to value, invest in and valorise NBS, providing holistic and transparent assessment of their monetary and non-monetary values. 
Objective 6: Strengthen and mobilise the CONEXUS collective capacity needed to develop NBS and improve sustainable urbanisation plans.</narrative>
  </description>
